From: noname <noname@example.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 06:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] raise the file descriptor limit before the stream starts

A driven r0.53 session at 1280x720 ended at committed=901 dropped=0 with
"[AVHWFramesContext] Failed to export memory plane 0 (16): Too many open
files (24)" and 1024 entries in /proc/PID/fd, the board's `sh -c "ulimit
-n"` soft limit; the hard one is 524288. 0023 stopped closing the
descriptor of a present the stream window already had a cached wl_buffer
for, because closing it revoked the descriptor the decoder holds for that
surface and the next pull answers "fstat on DMA-BUF failed: Bad file
descriptor (os error 9)". So each of those presents leaves one descriptor
open that nothing else will close. The dma-buf objects behind them are the
ten-odd capture surfaces the V4L2 pool reuses, so VmRSS stayed at 188-238
MB while the count climbed with frames: 1024 descriptors bought 900 frames,
17 seconds of picture. Raising the soft limit to 65536 (legal below the
hard 524288) buys about 20 minutes at 52 fps, the length of the held
streams the README still marks as owed.

Greppable markers: opennow-fd-limit, wayland-video fps
---
--- a/opennow-qt/src/main.cpp
+++ b/opennow-qt/src/main.cpp
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 #include <clocale>
 #include <langinfo.h>
+#include <sys/resource.h>
 #include <QDebug>
 
 // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@ -29,8 +30,47 @@
     qInfo("OpenNOW: character type was %s, using en_US.UTF-8", codeset.constData());
 }
 
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// Enough open descriptors for a long stream
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+//
+// A frame whose DMA-BUF the stream window already cached is presented without
+// sending its descriptor in a request, and the streamer keeps the descriptors
+// of the decoder's own capture surfaces alive (opennow-diag: dma-buf export
+// handles kept alive at handoff), so neither side closes the descriptor such a
+// present arrives with and each of those presents leaves one more open. Measured
+// on r0.53 at 1280x720: the driven session ended at committed=901 dropped=0 with
+// "[AVHWFramesContext] Failed to export memory plane 0 (16): Too many open files
+// (24)" and 1024 entries in /proc/PID/fd, the board's `sh -c "ulimit -n"`. What
+// leaks is descriptor numbers, not capture memory: the V4L2/hantro pool reuses
+// the same ten-odd surfaces, so VmRSS stayed at 188-238 MB across the run, while
+// 1024 descriptors bought only 900 frames, about 17 seconds of picture. The
+// kernel's hard limit is 524288, so raising the soft one is legal; 65536 is
+// about 20 minutes of play at 52 fps, the length of the held streams this layer
+// still marks as owed to a session.
+static void widenDescriptorLimit()
+{
+    struct rlimit current {};
+    if (getrlimit(RLIMIT_NOFILE, &current) != 0)
+        return;
+    rlim_t wanted = 65536;
+    if (current.rlim_cur >= wanted)
+        return;
+    if (current.rlim_max != RLIM_INFINITY && current.rlim_max < wanted)
+        wanted = current.rlim_max;
+    if (wanted <= current.rlim_cur)
+        return;
+    struct rlimit raised { wanted, current.rlim_max };
+    if (setrlimit(RLIMIT_NOFILE, &raised) != 0)
+        return;
+    qInfo("opennow-fd-limit: the file descriptor limit was raised from %llu to %llu",
+          static_cast<unsigned long long>(current.rlim_cur),
+          static_cast<unsigned long long>(wanted));
+}
+
 int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 {
     preferUtf8CharacterType();
+    widenDescriptorLimit();
     return runApplication(argc, argv);
 }

